# apps/mobile — local environment. Copy to `.env` and edit.
#
# Every EXPO_PUBLIC_* variable is INLINED AT BUILD TIME, not read at run time.
# In SDK 57 babel-preset-expo's `inline-env-vars` plugin replaces each literal
# `process.env.EXPO_PUBLIC_…` with its value while Metro bundles, so:
#   - changing a value here needs the bundler restarted (`expo start -c`);
#   - the value ends up in the shipped JavaScript, so never put a secret in one;
#   - an EAS build does not upload this file (`.easignore` excludes `.env*`),
#     which is why `eas.json` sets the value per profile: `preview` points at
#     the demo API, `production` at the production API, and `development`
#     sets nothing, so a dev client bundles against this file on your machine.
#
# `src/lib/env.ts` is the only reader, and it throws at import when the value
# is missing, so a build without it crashes at launch rather than at the first
# request.

# The API origin, no trailing slash and no `/api/v1`. A phone cannot reach
# `localhost` on your laptop: use the laptop's LAN address (it moves with the
# DHCP lease). An Android emulator can use http://10.0.2.2:8000 and `expo start
# --web` can use http://localhost:8000.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.1.10:8000
